# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props shape name: `{ComponentName}Props`
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` for unions, intersections, and simple aliases; use `interface` for extensible object shapes when it reads better. For props, keep the name `{ComponentName}Props` and follow the neighboring file's existing pattern.
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Examples

- Props via `type`: `type ContextMenuProps = { ... }`
- Props via `interface`: `interface LayerUIProps { ... }`
- Non-props alias: `type AppProps = Merge<...>`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## How to verify

- ESLint and types: `yarn test:code` and `yarn test:typecheck` from the repo root.
- Named exports: spot-check new modules for `export default`; align with neighboring files in the same directory (this repo prefers named exports for components).
- Colocation: new components should ship with or update `ComponentName.test.tsx` next to the component when behavior changes (see `testing.mdc`).
- Props/type-vs-interface: in PR review, compare the new declaration with nearby files in the same folder and ensure the chosen form matches this rule and the examples above; there is no repo rule that all props must be `type` or all props must be `interface`.
